It also explained that the Nyquist Sampling Theorem requires the sampling frequency to be at least twice the highest frequency contained in the signal. For the 10 Hz signal, the theoretical minimum sampling frequency is therefore 20 Hz.

ChatGPT also explained that aliasing occurs when the sampling frequency is too low and causes the sampled signal to appear as a different frequency.

